\section{Time conventions}{

All lengths are whole days. The pregnancy start date is \strong{day 0} and the outcome date is
day \code{GA}, where \verb{GA = outcome date - start date} (\code{GA_event_days_final}); for example, a
pregnancy that starts on 1 January and ends on 8 January has \code{GA = 7} (1+0 weeks).
Completed weeks are \code{floor(GA / 7)} (\code{GA_event_week_final}): days 0-6 are week 0, and day 154
is 22+0 weeks. The Norwegian registries' statistics count weeks ordinally (week \code{n} = days \code{7(n-1)} to
\verb{7n-1}), so "before week 9" in the Registry of Pregnancy Termination means \code{GA <= 55} days.
"Within \code{d} days before the outcome" means \verb{0 <= outcome date - record date <= d}.
}

